  "details": "*This feedback is being submitted on behalf of my friend.\n\nWhen EAC (Easy Anti-Cheat) finishes loading and waits for the game window to launch, the VRChat game window does not appear after the EAC window disappears. At the same time, Steam can no longer detect that VRChat is running (the status changes from \"In-Game\" to \"Online\"). However, both the EAC and VRChat processes still appear in Task Manager, with the VRChat process showing almost no resource usage.\n\nAfter testing, it was found that directly opening VRChat.exe (bypassing EAC) allows the VRChat game window to launch and run normally. Launching the game through luncher.exe results in the same issue, and Steam fails to detect VRChat running at all.\n\nMethods already attempted:\n\nVerifying file integrity\n\nUninstalling and reinstalling EAC\n\nReinstalling the game\n\nRepairing runtime libraries\n\nRepairing the system\n\nRestarting the computer\n\nTroubleshooting network issues\n\nSwitching game versions\n\nNone of these solutions worked.\n\nUsing mechanical translation",
